Usage:
   BIND infile<.exe> doscalls.lib (file.lib..) (file.obj..)
	(-o outfile<.exe>) (-m <mapfile>) (-n name..) (-n @file)

 Where infile is the name of the exe file
       file.lib & file.obj are additional modules to bind
       -o outfile is the name of the bound exe (default is infile)
       -n name.. list of names to map to BadDynLink function
       -n @file is a file of names to map
       -m leave linker map file in outfile.bm
       mapfile is the name of the linker map file

 Key: Parameters in () are optional, but must be entered as shown
      and those in <> are optional.

EXIT
